    code: { lang: "python", title: "header_and_ports.py — analyzer + lab port check (complete; run ONLY against your lab)", code: "import re, socket, sys\nimport requests\n\ndef analyze_headers(url):\n    try:\n        r = requests.get(url, timeout=5)\n    except requests.RequestException as e:\n        print(f'Request failed: {e}'); return\n    print(f'{url} -> HTTP {r.status_code}')\n    for h in ['Strict-Transport-Security', 'Content-Security-Policy',\n              'X-Content-Type-Options', 'Referrer-Policy']:\n        print(f\"  {h}: {'present' if h in r.headers else 'MISSING'}\")\n    ips = re.findall(r'\\d{1,3}(?:\\.\\d{1,3}){3}', r.text)\n    if ips: print('  IPs mentioned in body:', sorted(set(ips)))\n\ndef check_ports(host, ports):\n    for port in ports:\n        try:\n            with socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=2) as s:\n                s.settimeout(2)\n                try: banner = s.recv(80).decode(errors='replace').strip()\n                except socket.timeout: banner = '(no banner)'\n                print(f'  {host}:{port} OPEN  {banner}')\n        except OSError:\n            print(f'  {host}:{port} closed/filtered')\n\ntarget = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'http://localhost:8000'\nanalyze_headers(target)\nprint('Port check — your lab host only (192.168.56.10):')\ncheck_ports('192.168.56.10', [22, 80, 443])", output: "http://localhost:8000 -> HTTP 200\n  Strict-Transport-Security: MISSING\n  Content-Security-Policy: MISSING\n  X-Content-Type-Options: present\n  Referrer-Policy: MISSING\nPort check — your lab host only (192.168.56.10):\n  192.168.56.10:22 OPEN  SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_9.6\n  192.168.56.10:80 closed/filtered\n  192.168.56.10:443 closed/filtered", lines: ["timeout=5 on every request: a dead server becomes a handled exception, not a hang.", "Header lookup is case-insensitive in requests (a CaseInsensitiveDict) — 'present' logic is safe.", "The regex finds IPv4-shaped strings in the body; set() deduplicates before sorting.", "create_connection + recv reads a banner; OSError covers refused AND filtered — the tool honestly cannot tell them apart at this level."] },
    mistakes: ["Omitting timeouts — the #1 reliability bug in beginner network tools.", "Scanning a host you do not own 'just to test the script' — unauthorized, logged, and unnecessary: your lab VM exists for this.", "Trusting a regex's matches as validated IPs (999.1.1.1 matches the shape; validate ranges if it matters)."],
    security: "These three projects (header analyzer, status checker, inventory tool) are portfolio-grade — when pointed at your own lab with a written scope note attached. The authorization note is part of the deliverable, not fine print.",
    pc: ["Serve a folder with python -m http.server 8000, run the analyzer against localhost, and explain each MISSING line using Level 5.", "Point check_ports at your VirtualBox host-only VM and compare with ss -tlnp run inside it."],
